.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typing_extensions\&._allow_reckless_class_checks ( depth = \fC2\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Allow instance and class checks for special stdlib modules\&.
The abc and functools modules indiscriminately call isinstance() and
issubclass() on the whole MRO of a user class, which may contain protocols\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "typing_extensions\&._caller ( depth = \fC1\fP,  default = \fC'__main__'\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.SS "typing_extensions\&._check_generic ( cls,  parameters,  elen = \fC\fB_marker\fP\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Check correct count for parameters of a generic cls (internal helper)\&.

This gives a nice error message in case of count mismatch\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "typing_extensions\&._clean_optional ( obj,  hints,  globalns = \fCNone\fP,  localns = \fCNone\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.SS "typing_extensions\&._collect_parameters ( args)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Collect all type variables and parameter specifications in args
in order of first appearance (lexicographic order)\&.

For example::

    assert _collect_parameters((T, Callable[P, T])) == (T, P)

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "typing_extensions\&._collect_type_vars ( types,  typevar_types = \fCNone\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Collect all type variable contained in types in order of
first appearance (lexicographic order)\&. For example::

    _collect_type_vars((T, List[S, T])) == (T, S)

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "typing_extensions\&._concatenate_getitem ( self,  parameters)\fC [protected]\fP"

.SS "typing_extensions\&._could_be_inserted_optional ( t)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
detects Union[\&.\&.\&., None] pattern
